// Sentinel analytic rule - Entra ID sign-in brute force
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1110 (Brute Force)
// Data source : SigninLogs (Entra ID via the Microsoft Entra ID data connector)
// Signal      : ResultType 50126 = "invalid username or password" - the exact code a
//               password-guessing attack generates. Filtering on it drops MFA failures
//               and conditional-access blocks from the alert scope.
// Threshold   : 5 failures/hour per user+IP. Above normal typo rates, and below Entra
//               smart lockout's default of 10 - so the rule fires while failures still
//               return 50126 (after lockout they shift to 50053 and this signal goes quiet).
// Deployment  : the ago(1h) filter below is for running this interactively in Logs
//               (as in the screenshots). In the scheduled analytic rule, remove it and
//               set the lookback in the rule configuration - hardcoding both can miss
//               events when ingestion is delayed.
// Entities    : in the rule config, IPAddress maps to the IP entity and
//               UserPrincipalName to the Account entity, which is what the playbook
//               reads from the incident.

SigninLogs
| where ResultType == "50126"
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)
| summarize FailedAttempts = count() by UserPrincipalName, IPAddress, Location
| where FailedAttempts > 5
| project UserPrincipalName, IPAddress, Location, FailedAttempts
| order by FailedAttempts desc
